## Three independent licensing questions

| Subject | Governed by | Status |
|---|---|---|
| **Software** | `LICENSE` | MIT — **provisional default, requires confirmation** |
| **Documentation** | not yet decided | The governance documents in `docs/` are substantial original work and may warrant separate terms (for example CC-BY) |
| **Public scientific data** | the source's own terms, per record | Recorded in the provenance schema `license` field (`ADR-0003`, `SCI0-003`) |

These do not follow from one another. An MIT-licensed codebase does not license the data
it ingests, and redistributing a snapshot is governed by the source terms — ChEMBL,
BindingDB, PubChem and RCSB PDB each impose their own.

## Data redistribution

No dataset is committed to this repository (ENG §13; `data/` is DVC-tracked and
git-ignored). Snapshots are content-hashed artefacts held outside version control, and any
redistribution is subject to the per-record licence recorded in provenance, not to the
terms above.

